# Provisional affine-pentagon thesis extension

This four-page standalone draft preserves the new result and complete pentagon-specific argument in reader-facing source. **It has no human prose acceptance and is not integrated into the active thesis.** The user explicitly authorized a provisional writeup to preserve knowledge, while retaining the short rotation proof and keeping ten-facet local maximality separate.

- `section.tex`: extension section, no document wrapper; unique `pentagon-affine` labels.
- `standalone.tex`: preview wrapper using the existing bibliography.
- `build.sh`: build from any working directory.
- `standalone.pdf`: generated local preview, ignored by Git and reproducible.

## Mathematical authority and scope

The maintained complete research account is `formal/pentagon-affine-products/research.tex`. The immutable Pro return is `docs/pro-handoffs/pentagon-return/received/math/research.tex`; the independent principal-proof audit is `docs/pro-handoffs/pentagon-return/audit-affine.md`. The parent integration packet records the imported Haim–Kislev convention check. No novelty claim is made here.

The draft derives the exact capacity, sharp systolic bound and equality classification for **independent invertible linear images of regular pentagons**. Translation invariance extends this to affine images. It does not claim optimality for arbitrary pentagons or all ten-facet polytopes. Matrix containment excludes better six-group competitors; it does not exclude tied six-group maximizers.

The proof follows the Pro argument but specializes the four-group hull directly to pentagons, avoiding the general difference-body lemma. A sparse maximizer exists; the five closure triples supply all four-group generators; two matrix identities and the twelve-order symmetry reduction cover all six-group competitors. Area containment of the decagon proves the ratio and equality classification.

